CHAPTER.VERS:
Moreover concerning a 

          He means such as should be turned from their idolatry to serve the true God.
         stranger, that [is] not of thy people Israel, but cometh out of a far country for thy name's sake;

[Yet] if they shall bethink themselves in the land whither they were carried captives, and repent, and make supplication unto thee 

          Though the temple was the chief place of prayer, yet he does not exclude them who being forced by necessity to call upon him in other places.
         in the land of them that carried them captives, saying, We have sinned, and have done perversely, we have committed wickedness;
